    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by the elite-tier production expected from **Kyle Tucker** (85.09) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.87). **Kyle Tucker** benefits significantly from the matchup against Gibson, whose poor 5.63 xERA offers a massive ceiling for extra-base hits. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play for the SB category; he faces the slow delivery of Sasaki, which boosts his scoring efficiency to near-elite levels. Both **Andy Pages** (71.49) and **Josh Jung** (63.35) capitalize on favorable SP matchups, providing a strong core that should sustain our offensive floor throughout the slate.\n\nPlatoon edges and matchup context have heavily influenced today\u2019s configuration. **Nolan Schanuel** (62.53) gets the nod over several bench options due to a strong combination of park factors and the +10% efficiency gain from the matchup against Springs, while **Liam Hicks** (51.03) and **Brayan Rocchio** (55.82) are deployed primarily to exploit dynamic platoon advantages against right-handed pitching. The closest decision on our bench involved **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (53.71), who remained on the pine despite a decent 53.71 score; he was ultimately pushed out by the superior power-projection and lineup positioning of the starters ahead of him. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's matchups. **Jackson Merrill** (52.45) draws a difficult assignment against deGrom, whose ability to control the run game (-2% SB penalty) complicates our focus on speed. Similarly, both **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** face Misiorowski, a pitcher with an elite 2.70 xERA that significantly dampens their offensive outlook today. We are monitoring all lineups closely, as any sudden changes in the batting order could necessitate a quick pivot to ensure we maximize our daily efficiency and preserve our game caps effectively.",
